From: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: msgbuf: do not wait for tx status on the BCM4377

The BCM4377 firmware returns the tx status of the queued packets only
when it gets the flowring delete request, before the delete response.
brcmf_msgbuf_delete_flowring() waits up to 100 ms for them before it
sends the request, so every disconnect logs a timeout.

Send the delete right away on the BCM4377. Its tx status still comes
before the delete response, so pend_8021x_cnt drains as before. Other
chips keep the wait.

Also reset the outstanding counter when the ring is created, as upstream
commit ae13aa2ec885 ("wifi: brcmfmac: msgbuf: count tx status only for
the current flowring") does. A wait that times out on other chips no
longer leaves it below zero for the next ring with the same flowid.

Tested-by: Yossef Osman <Yossef.Osman@proton.me>
Signed-off-by: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>

---
index 8e5c697..1ec920a 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
 
 #include <brcmu_utils.h>
 #include <brcmu_wifi.h>
+#include <brcm_hw_ids.h>
 
 #include "core.h"
 #include "debug.h"
@@ -645,6 +646,7 @@ brcmf_msgbuf_flowring_create_worker(struct brcmf_msgbuf *msgbuf,
 	brcmf_commonring_config(msgbuf->flowrings[flowid],
 				BRCMF_H2D_TXFLOWRING_MAX_ITEM,
 				BRCMF_H2D_TXFLOWRING_ITEMSIZE, dma_buf);
+	atomic_set(&msgbuf->flowrings[flowid]->outstanding_tx, 0);
 
 	commonring = msgbuf->commonrings[BRCMF_H2D_MSGRING_CONTROL_SUBMIT];
 	brcmf_commonring_lock(commonring);
@@ -1478,8 +1480,13 @@ void brcmf_msgbuf_delete_flowring(struct brcmf_pub *drvr, u16 flowid)
 	flow->rings[flowid]->status = RING_CLOSING;
 	brcmf_commonring_unlock(commonring_del);
 
-	/* wait for commonring txflow finished */
-	while (retry && atomic_read(&commonring_del->outstanding_tx)) {
+	/*
+	 * Wait for commonring txflow finished. The BCM4377 firmware returns
+	 * the tx status of the posted packets only on the delete request,
+	 * before the delete response.
+	 */
+	while (drvr->bus_if->chip != BRCM_CC_4377_CHIP_ID && retry &&
+	       atomic_read(&commonring_del->outstanding_tx)) {
 		usleep_range(5000, 10000);
 		retry--;
 	}
